# {{ .Name }} ({{ .Type | title }})

Provides a resource for configuring the Bastion's global SMTP server settings, used to send
system emails (notifications, alerts, etc.).

## Example Usage

```terraform
resource "wallix-bastion_config_smtp" "main" {
  protocol              = "starttls"
  authentication_method = "plain"
  server                = "smtp.example.com"
  port                  = 587
  postmaster_email      = "postmaster@example.com"
  sender_name           = "WALLIX Bastion"
  sender_email          = "bastion@example.com"
  user                  = "smtp-user"
  password              = var.smtp_password
}
```

{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

## Usage Notes

### Singleton Configuration

There is only one SMTP configuration on the Bastion. This resource always manages that single,
global configuration rather than creating a new one — importing or destroying it never removes
the underlying configuration on the Bastion (there is no delete endpoint for it), it only stops
Terraform from managing it.

### Mandatory Fields

The Bastion API requires `protocol`, `authentication_method`, `server`, `postmaster_email`,
`sender_name`, and `sender_email` to be set together on every update, confirmed empirically
against a live Bastion — attempting to update only a subset of these returns a
"Missing mandatory parameters" error, even though the field descriptions don't call this out
explicitly.

### Credentials

`password` is sensitive and is never returned by the API on read — Terraform will always show it
as configured but the value can't be verified by reading back state.

## Import

The SMTP configuration can be imported using any ID (it is always stored as `smtpConfig` in
state, since the API doesn't provide one), e.g.

```shell
terraform import wallix-bastion_config_smtp.main smtpConfig
```
